    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d403">

                <pb facs="0539" n="471" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg471"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Burlingame</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 196.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1867-04-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 5, 1867.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I enclose herewith a copy of a letter and
                    of its accompaniment, which on the 18th of March was addressed to this
                    department by the Hon. J. E. Stuart, in relation to the completion of the
                    enterprise of the East India Telegraph Company.</p>
                <p>You are instructed that while committing this government to no preference or
                    favor over all other similar undertakings existing or to come, you will use your
                    good offices in promoting the object sought.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anson Burlingame</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d403-a1.xml" xpointer="d403-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
